RoguePM - rogued project notes: 
    use sled::{Db, Tree, IVec};

    pub fn init_database(path: &str) -> sled::Result<Db> {
        sled::open(path)
    }

    pub fn set(tree: &Tree, key: impl AsRef<[u8]>, value: impl AsRef<[u8]>) -> sled::Result<Option<IVec>> {
        tree.insert(key, value)
    }

    pub fn get(tree: &Tree, key: impl AsRef<[u8]>) -> sled::Result<Option<IVec>> {
        tree.get(key)
    }

    pub fn delete(tree: &Tree, key: impl AsRef<[u8]>) -> sled::Result<Option<IVec>> {
        tree.remove(key)
    }

    pub fn dump_tree(tree: &Tree) -> sled::Result<Vec<(IVec, IVec)>> {
        tree.iter().collect::<sled::Result<Vec<_>>>()
    }

What it stores
1. Own identity (my_identity) — device_id, TLS cert+key, SSH keypair. Generated once, survives restarts.
2. Paired peers (paired/{device_id}) — hostname, IP, pairing timestamp. Loaded into memory on startup so previously paired peers are known immediately (even before mDNS rediscovers them).
3. TLS cert pinning (paired/{id}.cert_fingerprint) — TOFU (Trust On First Use): on first pair, the peer's TLS cert fingerprint is stored. Future connections verify the fingerprint to detect MITM.
4. Peer project lists (peer_lists/{device_id}) — remote peers' project paths, synced during pairing and periodically. Bash queries via rogue list --remote.
5. Own project list (my_list) — this machine's project paths for sharing with peers.
6. Path leases (leases/{path_hash}) — distributed path-locking: which peer holds a write lease on each exported path, with TTL.

Init sequence:
    1. Parse CLI args (clap) for --db-path, --port, --socket-path
    2. Open sled at ~/.rogued/Data/rogueData (expand ~ manually)
    3. Generate/load device_id from sled
    4. Load paired peers from sled into state
    5. Register mDNS service (add device_id to TXT properties)
    6. Spawn tcp_listener (tokio::spawn)
    7. Spawn handle_unix_sockets (tokio::spawn)
    8. discover_hosts — on ServiceResolved, if peer is Paired, call auto_connect
Unix socket dispatch — reworked to match on request type via serde:
    - ping → Pong!
    - discoverHost → return full peer table with states
    - pair { hostname } → lookup peer, call initiate_pair
    - accept { hostname } → call resolve_pending(hostname, true)
    - reject { hostname } → call resolve_pending(hostname, false)
    - pending → list pending requests
    - forget { hostname } → remove from paired + sled


makehuman2  project notes:
    1. opengl/camera.py     line 235 handles camera zoom 
    2. opengl/camera.py     line 381 handles camera rotation rotation(xAngle, yAngle)
            > Horizontal rotation (lines 395-397): Rotates the camera position around the cameraDir (up axis) using xAngle
            > Vertical rotation (lines 401-403): Rotates the resulting position around the rightVector using yAngle
            > Angles come from arcBallRotation (line 304-305): xAngle = (last_mousex - x) * deltaAngleX, yAngle = (last_mousey - y) * deltaAngleY
            > deltaAngleX = 2π / viewport_width, deltaAngleY = π / viewport_height (lines 419-420) — so a full drag across the screen = full 360° horizontal / 180° vertical rotation


